      "problem": "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2 \\csc x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we just take the constant out of the derivative and use the result for the derivative of $\\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x) \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
